## Console-only KaliAI build: no desktop at all. This is Stage B of the
## staged build-out (see DESIGN.md) — proves the kaliai CLI + kaliai-recon
## MCP server bake correctly into a real Kali image before layering the
## Hyprland desktop (variant-kaliai) back on top and debugging that
## separately. `kaliai agent` and kaliai-recon don't need a GUI to work.
##
## Built via: distro/build.sh --variant kaliai-min

## Live images always want this (kali-desktop-live is the desktop-specific
## one and is deliberately NOT included here — confirmed via Kali's own
## variant-minimal, which ships no package list at all, that a desktop meta-
## package isn't structurally required for a bootable live image).
kali-linux-core

## Metapackages
##   For the complete list see: https://www.kali.org/tools/kali-meta/
kali-linux-default

## KaliAI runtime deps — the kaliai CLI itself is installed by
## variant-kaliai-min/hooks/live/0020-kaliai-tooling.chroot, not apt.
python3-venv
python3-pip
rsync
